@startuml
title Support Families And Solver Interpretations
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 180
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

rectangle "Domain surfaces\n(topography + substratum)" as Surf
rectangle "Support constraints\nstream, ocean, zones,\ncatchment outline" as Cst

rectangle "Structured sgrid\nraster-aligned quads" as SGrid
rectangle "Catchment-conformal\nplanar mesh\ntriangles or polygons" as CMesh

rectangle "Repeated vertical layering" as Vert
rectangle "Layered SolverMesh\ncell centers, neighbors,\nlayer ids, support labels" as SolverMesh
rectangle "2D shallow-flow mesh\nnatural planar support" as BqMesh

rectangle "MODFLOW-NWT\nDIS on structured grid" as NWT
rectangle "MODFLOW 6\nDISV on layered mesh\nXT3D when needed" as MF6
rectangle "Boussinesq backend\nfinite-volume operators" as BQ

Surf --> SGrid
Surf --> CMesh
Cst --> SGrid : approximated by grid
Cst --> CMesh : followed more explicitly

SGrid --> Vert
CMesh --> Vert
Vert --> SolverMesh

SGrid --> NWT
SolverMesh --> MF6
CMesh --> BqMesh
BqMesh --> BQ

note bottom of SolverMesh
The same planar support can feed different
backends, but not with the same geometry
contract or the same numerical assumptions.
end note
@enduml
